# Failing-first: tests/fm-spawn-worktree-settle.test.sh test_allocator_claimed_clean_slot_lease_is_released (success and abort) fails on the base with a steering lease held on a clean claimed slot the reuse test refuses and passes on the fixed head; tests/fm-spawn-defer-slot.test.sh test_adopted_slot_with_unpushed_commits_is_not_returned keeps the abort path from returning an adopted claimed slot holding unpushed commits. Live with Treehouse v2.3.0 in a scratch pool before building: `treehouse get --lease --lease-holder fm-spawn-NEW --no-fetch` handed a claimed clean slot, fm_treehouse_reset_target resolved origin/release under a divergent base branch, fm_treehouse_slot_reusable refused it, and `treehouse status --json` showed the slot leased to fm-spawn-NEW with no processes; the rewritten-main case reproduced the same way, and `treehouse return --if-lease-holder fm-spawn-NEW` cleared that lease while leaving the other task's claim, the clean worktree, and branch refs intact.
